WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.600
Go, Giant Killer!

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:05.620
<i>Tetsuo and the class rep were defeated by IV.</i>

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.250
<i>Based on his true identity, he really is powerful!</i>

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.970
<i>If so... I will end this once and for all!</i>

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.660
Wait, his opponent is me!

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.250
Have you forgotten the face of your <i>greatest</i> fan...

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.670
IV!?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:27.950
Shark...!

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.100
I finally found you, IV!

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.370
Ryoga... I actually forgot...

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.620
You really are my biggest fan out there.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.210
Then allow me to repay the debt I owe you!

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.580
Debt, huh...?

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.920
Oh right, how's your "precious" younger sister doing?

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.240
Younger sister?

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.420
you set up everything...

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.220
It's all because of me... because of me...

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.800
She...

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.670
I will exact revenge on you here and now!

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.980
Shark... you... seek revenge?

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.010
Excellent. I really like people like you.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.150
This is....?

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.000
It's a Duel Anchor.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.940
You cannot escape without finishing the Duel with me!

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.980
III, this guy is my prey! Get lost!

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.970
Brother IV, Ryoga's deck doesn't have any Numbers.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.360
Therefore it won't be necessary for you to become his opponent, right?

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.450
Plus, Tron's order is absolute.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.690
The fanservice is over.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.000
Wait, stop! Are you going to run away, IV?

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.530
I already finished collecting my Heart Pieces.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.170
I will wait for you in the Finals.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.740
IV!

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.450
Calm down. My brother is quite busy.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.650
Plus, your opponent is me.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.060
<i>Just who are those people?</i>

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.590
<i>That's the same anchor Kaito uses.</i>

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:30.690
<i>Don't tell me these people are collecting Numbers as well with the same technical power of Kaito?</i>

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.870
Anyway, we have to get him to hospital!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:35.750
Right.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.110
Kotori, Tetsuo!

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:43.410
You can observe this Duel for yourself, and we won't have any problem on this side!

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.390
But...

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.340
Yuma... I agree with him as well.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.640
Astral...

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.730
I got it. Take care of him!

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.160
As you wish, I will clobber you first!

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.900
Here I go!

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.260
Duel Mode, Change!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.550
Duel Disk, set!

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.680
D-Gazer, set!

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.070
<i>AR Vision - Link established.</i>

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:27.410
Duel!!

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.240
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.040
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:42.540
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:51.220
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:56.770
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:02.480
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:07.360
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:12.870
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.620
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.240
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.340
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:29.800
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.340
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.300
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:40.940
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.400
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.400
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:55.280
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:00.270
Duel!!

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:08.200
"Number 34: The Determined Revenge,
The Tragic Duelist, Shark!"

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.910
I will go first. My turn, draw!

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.700
I activate the Field Magic, Deep Sea Monarchy - Sunken Kingdom!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.250
This card increases Water-Attribute Monster's Attack Power by 300 points!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.770
The field has gone underwater! Where's my oxygen tank?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.560
Yuma, this is AR space.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.980
I Summon OOparts Mayan Machine!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.700
Then I set a card face-down and end my turn!

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.620
What the heck are OOparts??

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.460
OOparts were art 'works' that were built in the ancient civilization with seemingly impossible technology at that time.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.880
Their existence was still wrapping under mysteries.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.470
My turn, draw!

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.890
I summon Hammer Shark!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:17.140
Then due to field magic, Sunken Kingdom's effect, Hammer Shark gains 300 ATK!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.230
Looks like you weren't aware that I use a Water-Attribute deck.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.940
But in the Field Magic, Sunken Kingdom,

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:30.780
you cannot attack OOparts Monsters with Level Four or lower Monsters.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.740
So that's your insurance, huh?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.950
But... Magic Card, Downward Current!

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:42.920
During this turn, this card can change my Monster's level from any number between 1 to 3!

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.210
I will decrease Hammer Shark's LV by 1!

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.050
You Duel so strangely.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.890
What exactly do you plan to do by lowering its level?

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.350
I special summon Big Jaws!

00:06:55.970 --> 00:07:00.730
When I use a Normal Magic card during this turn, Big Jaws can be special summoned from my hand!

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:07.690
Due to Sunken Kingdom's effect, Big Jaws will gain 300 ATK too!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.950
There are 2 LV 3 monsters...

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.240
I overlay the LV3 Hammer Shark and Big Jaws!

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:20.620
I build the Overlay Network with these 2 monsters!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.420
Xyz Summon!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.090
Come forth, Black Ray Lancer!

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:37.140
Xyz monsters don't have levels to begin with, so Sunken Kingdom's effect won't work!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.730
Nice one, Shark!

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:44.900
Go, Black Ray Lancer, attack Mayan Machine!

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.690
Black Spear!!

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.120
Trap, activate! Stonehenge Method!

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.790
With this card, when an OOparts monster was destroyed,

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:07.880
I can special summon 1 LV4 or lower OOparts monster from my deck in face-up defense position!

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.510
Come forth, OOparts Colossal Head!

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.850
I set one card, and end my turn.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.180
My turn, draw!

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.770
I summon OOparts Golden Shuttle!

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.740
Then I activate the Continuous Magic, Orichalcum Chain!

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.030
When this card is face-up on my field when I performed a Xyz summon,

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.910
I can use one less Overlay Unit.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:39.830
Say what?

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.410
But Orichalcum Chain has risks as well.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.540
When this card is destroyed,

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:50.380
The Xyz monster summoned by this effect will have its control switch to my opponent!

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:54.010
<i>Is he planning to take such risk for the sake of Xyz summoning?</i>

00:08:54.800 --> 00:09:01.140
I overlay LV 4 Colossal Head, Golden Shuttle and Orichalcum Chain's effect!!

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:07.100
I build the Overlay Network with these 2 monsters and Orichalcum Chain's effect!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.610
Xyz Summon!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.570
Show yourself, Number 32!

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:21.740
The biggest, most powerful ruler of the deep sea! Its sharp fang shall exterminate everything!

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:29.130
Sea Biting Dragon Shark Drake!

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:36.970
A Number!

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.100
Indeed he is...

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:41.640
So it finally appears.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:47.310
Due to the Sunken Kingdom's effect, Shark Drake gains 300 ATK!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:52.400
Go, Shark Drake! Attack Black Ray Lancer!

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.690
Depth Bite!!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.330
I activate Shark Drake's effect!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.840
When it destroys my opponent's monster by battle, once per turn, by detaching one overlay unit,

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:18.220
The destroyed monster will lose 1000 ATK, and special summon that target to my opponent's field!

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:23.350
And it can battle with that monster again!

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:27.640
So that Number can attack twice?

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:33.270
But it's more than just 'attack twice'. It's a very overpowered effect!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:39.570
It will bite you until you have no bones left! Shark Drake attacks Black Ray Lancer once again!

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.240
DEPTH BITE!

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:48.710
Shark!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.380
Hey! Are you alright?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.220
You shut up, Yuma!

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.090
Do you honestly think I would get defeated like this?

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:05.060
Then I set one card and end my turn!

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:10.850
Well, if you can't think of a way to counter Shark Drake, then you have no where to escape!

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.440
That Shark, if this continues...

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.820
But there is a way to bring a reversal under these circumstances.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.400
But that would require...

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.490
I need to take away his Number!

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.420
I need to take away his Number!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.460
My turn, draw!

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:37.090
I summon Skull Kraken!

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.140
I activate Skull Kraken's effect!

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.100
When this card is summoned successfully,

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:54.980
It can destroy one face-up Magic or Trap on my opponent's field!

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.150
I destroy Orichalcum's Chain!

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.950
Thus I gained the control of Shark Drake!

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.290
<i>That's right, that's how it should be...</i>

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.830
<i>That's the only thing you can do if you wish to survive.</i>

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:15.710
<i>My mission will...</i>

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:22.630
Shark!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:40.730
Alright, accept me, Ryouga.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:58.540
Accept me, and release the darkness inside your heart.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.010
<i>Shark!</i>

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.630
<i>Let's Duel again some time!</i>

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.010
<i>Let's bring it to 'em together!</i>

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:13.020
<i>Why?! Why would you give up Dueling?!</i>

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.560
<i>Didn't I already say we are fiends?!</i>

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.060
But...!

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:19.610
<i>DON'T LAUGH!</i>

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.480
<i>What's so darn funny?</i>

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.740
<i>What's so funny about having a fear of losing?</i>

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:32.200
<i>It must be the same for Shark. That's why Shark's duel, is for real!</i>

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:37.290
I'm not... the same as I used to be!

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.800
As if I'd ever be controlled by the likes of you!

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.640
Because I am who I am!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.850
So he finally surpassed the Numbers' power, huh?

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.140
Shark...

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.810
<i>He wasn't possessed by the Number?</i>

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.610
As long as I have this guy's power,

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:06.030
Go, Shark Drake! Attack him directly!

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.820
Yes! If this connects, he'll receive huge damage!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:14.080
I won't let that happen! Trap, activate! Antikythera Gear!

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:21.670
When there are 2 or more monsters on my opponent's field, and my opponent declares a direct attack,

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:26.340
I can gain control of the monster besides the attacking one, and put it in defense position!

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:30.140
Dream on! Trap Card, Hyper Water Pressure!

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:37.560
With this card, by destroying one monster on my field, I am allowed to draw one card from my deck!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.230
Now your trap is useless!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:45.940
Resume your attack, Shark Drake!

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.960
I set 2 cards face-down, and end my turn.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:06.590
<i>Nice one. My mission is give him the Numbers.</i>

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:12.010
<i>Although Tron said after the mission is completed, feel free to lose purposely...</i>

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.220
<i>But don't get too overconfident, Ryoga!</i>

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.930
My turn, draw!

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.980
I activate Magic card, OOparts Technology!

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:29.900
By banishing one OOparts monster from my graveyard,

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:34.030
I can draw 2 cards from my graveyard, and send one card to my graveyard.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.910
I special summon OOparts Crystal Bone!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:44.250
When only my opponent controls a monster, I can special summon it from my hand!

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:52.180
When this card is special summoned this way, I can also special summon OOparts Crystal Skull from my graveyard!

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.350
Revive, Crystal Skull!

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:03.690
I overlay the LV3 Crystal Bone and Crystal Skull!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.980
I build the Overlay Network with these 2 monsters!

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:10.820
Xyz Summon!

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.280
Show yourself, OOparts Crystal Alien!

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.500
With this card, by detaching 1 overlay unit,

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:27.590
It cannot be destroyed by battle during this turn and the battle damage inflicted to this card will inflict to my opponent instead!

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:28.130
What?!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:34.640
In other words, the difference of ATK between your Shark Drake and my OOparts Alien is 1000,

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.640
You shall receive damage equal to that value!

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:41.810
Go, Crystal Alien, attack Shark Drake!

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.890
REFLECT FLASH!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.860
Shoot! If this attack connects...

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:48.480
It's over, Ryouga!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.690
Quick-Play Magic, Plate Salvage!

00:16:55.530 --> 00:17:00.290
Plate Salvage negates the effect of Field Spell for 2 turns!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.630
Awesome! Now we are finally above sea level!

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.880
Now Sunken Kingdom's effect disappears!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:17.890
Shark Drake's ATK will return to 2800!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:39.200
Amazing. By negating Field Spell's effect, he decreased Shark Drake's ATK to preserve his LP!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.450
But... both Shark and III have only 300 LP left.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.910
The next blow will decide the outcome.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.920
<i>He actually survived Crystal Alien's Reflect Flash.</i>

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:53.670
<i>But, he will definitely use Shark Drake's effect in his next turn,</i>

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.840
<i>The outcome will be decided at that moment!</i>

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:59.010
I set one card and end my turn!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.560
My turn, draw!

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.640
I attack Crystal Alien with Shark Drake!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.150
DEPTH BITE!!

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.770
Yes! Now it's Shark's win.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:16.610
Not yet, I activate OOparts monster Colossal Head's effect!

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.660
By banish this card from my graveyard,

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:23.910
I switch one monster on my field from Attack position to defense position!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:28.870
Darn!

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:33.340
Not good! His LP won't be depleted if his monster was in defense position!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.210
No...

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:38.680
But at this moment, I activate Shark Drake's effect!

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:46.810
When it destroys my opponent's monster by battle, by detaching one Overlay unit, that monster loses 1000 ATK,

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:50.480
And special summons itself to my opponent's field!

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:57.070
Do you think I would forget Shark Drake's effect?

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.400
Go, Shark Drake!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.700
Fortunately I haven't underestimated you one bit.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:07.950
I knew you would be able to control this Number!

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:11.630
Trap, activate! OOpart Ley Line Power!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:12.460
What?

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:18.090
With this card, when a monster was special summoned during the Battle Phase and battles,

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.760
I switch the ATK of the battling monsters!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:25.970
Now Crystal Alien and Shark Drake's ATK are exchanged!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.480
Then I win the duel!

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.060
As I expected.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:34.230
I am the fortunate one for not underestimating you.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:39.360
I knew you would expect me to use Shark Drake's effect.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:43.740
Trap activate! Deep Sea Lord's Judgment!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:48.540
This card negates the effect of the trap activated during Battle Phase!

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:49.870
How could that be?

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:56.670
Damn!

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:59.970
Resume your attack, Shark Drake!

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.990
Great, Shark won!

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:24.280
What a breathtaking exchange of offense and defense!

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:28.290
I see, you are quite good.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.790
I lost to you for today.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:37.000
But I am going to the Finals. It won't be easy for you if we meet next time!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:40.380
So that guy finished collecting Heart Pieces as well?

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:46.680
You can keep that Number. Consider it as a reward for winning this duel.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:54.060
He disappeared?

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:58.110
<i>Yuma!</i>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.020
Kotori!

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:03.200
I'm in the Hospital right now. The class rep is holding up for the moment.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.950
Good. I'll come over there as well!

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:08.240
Shark!

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.450
Yuma, don't get involved with me anymore...

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.290
Shark... something about revenge...

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:20.300
Shark!

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:25.550
<i>He acquired a Number once again... That means sooner or later, these two will...</i>

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.930
Good job, III.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:37.440
You always successfully complete the tasks I assigned you.

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:41.400
I just do everything I can for you, Tron.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:43.780
Looks like modesty is one of your virtues as well.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:44.740
But...

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:48.570
Ryoga wasn't possessed by the Number.

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:51.330
No, that's not the case.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:57.370
The darkness that sleeps inside people's hearts...

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:02.300
As long as there is even the tiniest of openings...

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:07.470
It will slowly expand without them realizing...

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:23.230
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:28.740
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:34.870
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.290
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.590
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.590 --> 00:22:45.550
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:48.470
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:52.760
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:56.310
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:59.520
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:06.150
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.360
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:13.780
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:15.540
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:17.950
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:23.040
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:26.880
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:29.590
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:34.010
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:35.970
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:37.850
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:40.810 --> 00:23:45.860
Photos that can display the future? Plus that future can be twisted according to his wish.

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:48.900
Could such a phenomenon really exist?

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:50.860
Geez, I won't care about Yuma anymore!

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:52.320
Maybe it was due to Numbers!

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:54.200
Kotori, where are you?

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:56.530
The power to manipulate future...

00:23:56.530 --> 00:24:01.710
As long as I beat this guy, and take away his Numbers, then the 'reality' shown in the pictures can also be corrected, right?

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:04.040
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:07.170
"The Shocking Scoop! Kotori's Dangerous Future!"

00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:09.300
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:13.050
Let's review the rules of the Duel Carnival!

00:24:13.510 --> 00:24:16.680
You have three days to qualify. The city venue is all of Heartland.

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:19.270
Always stand when challenged by a duel!

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:24.150
If 5 heart pieces are collected and a heart is completed, it's a final tournament advance!
